{"accounts":{"guide-entry-0a8338e2dc9d1cc76d9fea1e":{"description":"1st session of the International Law Commission (1949) Table of equivalents as between the Articles of the Declaration of the Rights and Duties of Nations Adopted by the American Institute of International Law and the Draft Declaration on the Rights and Duties of States proposed by the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Panama A/CN.4/11","document_locator":null,"document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-0a8338e2dc9d1cc76d9fea1e","section":"other"},"guide-entry-9bd7394e674c2e36ea6325b7":{"description":"1st session of the International Law Commission (1949) Draft Declaration on the Rights and Duties of States — As proposed by the Sub-Committee on the draft Declaration A/CN.4/W.5 (in Yearbook, 1949 , 19th meeting (12 May 1949), ft. 2)","document_locator":null,"document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-9bd7394e674c2e36ea6325b7","section":"working_group_or_subcommittee"},"guide-entry-a5f7e5211bf25580d9376825":{"description":"International Law Commission ( 1st session , 1949) Decided to submit the draft Declaration to the General Assembly stating that it was for the Assembly to decide what further course of action should be taken in relation to the draft Declaration and, in particular, whether it should be transmitted to Member Governments for comments. ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, part II, para.53 Yearbook, 1949","document_locator":"part II, para","document_role":"related_evidence","entry_id":"guide-entry-a5f7e5211bf25580d9376825","section":"final_outcome"},"guide-entry-c52352183f95758e88eaebb9":{"description":"Report of the International Law Commission on the work of its first session , 12 April to 19 June 1949 On the basis of the draft declaration presented by Panama and several related documents the Commission prepared the draft Declaration on Rights and Duties of States in the form of fourteen articles with commentaries . The Commission observed that \"the rights and duties set forth in the draft Declaration are formulated in general terms, without restriction or exception, as befits a declaration of basic rights and duties. The articles of the draft Declaration enunciate general principles of international law, the extent and the modalities of the application of which are to be determined by more precise rules.\" Discussion in plenary : 7th , 8th , 9th , 10th , 11th , 12th , 13th , 14th , 15th and 16th meetings (21 April to 5 May 1949), 19th , 20th , 21st , 22nd , 23rd , 24th and 25th meetings (12 to 23 May 1949), and 29th and 30th meetings (27 to 31 May 1949) ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, part II, paras. 44–53 Yearbook, 1949","document_locator":"part II, paras","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-c52352183f95758e88eaebb9","section":"ilc_report"},"guide-entry-d2fa6a90efed45b12fa801f6":{"description":"Draft Declaration on the Rights and Duties of States — Summary of action taken by the Commission after third reading of the Draft A/CN.4/W.8 (in Yearbook, 1949 , 23rd meeting (19 May 1949), ft. 1)","document_locator":null,"document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-d2fa6a90efed45b12fa801f6","section":"other"},"guide-entry-f51cddca54a6cd29502e9f14":{"description":"1st session of the International Law Commission (1949) Preparatory Study concerning a draft Declaration on the Rights and Duties of States A/CN.4/2 and Add.1 (United Nations publications, Sales No.: 1949.V.4) ILC Report, A/925 (A/4/10), 1949, part II, para. 45","document_locator":"part II, para","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-f51cddca54a6cd29502e9f14","section":"secretariat_and_secretary_general"},"guide-entry-f5d43250ddfb52c0f5c78eb6":{"description":"Draft Declaration on the Rights and Duties of States — Summary of action taken by the Commission with regard to the Draft (A/CN.4/2) A/CN.4/W.2 and Rev.1–4 (mimeograph)","document_locator":null,"document_role":"mentioned_in_description","entry_id":"guide-entry-f5d432